# [National Comparison of Ambulatory Physician Electronic Health Record Use Across Specialties]

- **Citation:** Holmgren AJ, Sinsky CA, Rotenstein L, et al. National Comparison of Ambulatory Physician Electronic Health Record Use Across Specialties. J Gen Intern Med. 2024. doi:10.1007/s11606-024-08930-4
- **Read by:** [Jessica], [28 October 2027]
- **Peer-reviewed?** yes (Q1 journal)

**What they did:** Cross-sectional study of Epic EHR usage metadata (Nov 2021 to Apr 2022), 200,081 ambulatory physicians at 396 organizations; EHR time normalized per 8 scheduled patient hours.

**Main result:** Physicians spent 5.8 h in the EHR per 8 h of patient time; documentation was the largest share (2.3 h). Varied by specialty (infectious disease 8.4 h vs orthopedics 3.3 h). 

**Limitation:** US only, one EHR vendor; measures time, not quality or document-handling tasks specifically. 

**Relevance to our project:** Shows the size of the documentation burden that automated document handling (like specialty routing) could reduce. 
